  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "unverified": "No cenote of El Punto has a position taken on site: the database only has Gerrard's 'El Punto - Punto Soliman' point (validity unknown), and Sentry, Ka'tu A'k, I'ch and Alberca have none; the map has no scale bar and is schematic. The placement is a best guess from the shapes of the water near Gerrard's point (the caleta at Bahia Soliman, the pond south of it, the bay's shore).",
  "placementWhy": "Guess (unverified): free similarity fit on four points, residuals 8, 19, 16 and 34 m; 0.305 m/px, map turned 6.4 degrees. Sentry Cenote, a long pool running east then turning north, on the caleta at the head of the lagoon north of Bahia Soliman (its west arm then the turn north into the lagoon; Gerrard's 'El Punto - Punto Soliman' point is at that turn): its west tip on the arm's west tip and its corner on the arm's turn (both read on the Mapbox/Maxar imagery). Cenote I'CH on the dark pond south of the caleta (OSM water way 1100734981), the one reached by a path from the dirt road as the database's directions say. The line's end at the sea (p. 0) on the top of the bulge of Bahia Soliman's north shore (OSM coastline vertex; the map draws the outlet at such a bulge, with the sea to the south). The four don't fit one similarity well (I'CH is the worst, 34 m): the map's Sentry-to-I'CH distance is about twice the caleta-to-pond one compared with the rest. Tried first: I'CH on the pond and the outlet on the shore alone (0.37 m/px, north kept): the lines then cross the caleta's open water twice, which the map, drawing every pool, doesn't show - rejected. At 0.305 m/px the drawn lines measure about 680 m against the 1,216 m (3,990 ft) the title gives: Mafia line plots are smoothed, and the stated length may include lines not drawn - a second sign the placement is approximate. K'a Tu A'ak falls on the wooded spit between the lagoon and the sea, Alberca by the beach houses: neither can be checked on the imagery. Nearest placed maps: Yax Muul (1.1 km west), Nohoch Nah Chich and the Sac Aktun Google plots (over 1 km): no overlap.",
